     0.1.42 re-check on an R9700 (Linux, ROCm 7.14), 12 prompts of 1.5K-24K tokens, first-token KL against the FP16 prompt path (MMQ / fused): IQ3_S 0.00332 / 0.00284, top-1 12 of 12 for both; IQ3_XXS 0.00335 / 0.00452 on one sample and 0.00344 / 0.00323 on a second (24 prompts pooled: 0.00340 / 0.00388, top-1 24 of 24 for both); the Q2_0 pack does not take these kernels on gfx12 (output bit-identical to MMQ). Because the IQ3_XXS pool is not at or below MMQ's, the flag stays opt-in. Measured on Linux only.
     gfx1200 builds the same kernels and was not run; Windows and K-quant packs (`STRATA_PF_FUSED_KQ=1`) were not measured.
+- **Exact defaults (arch table):** on gfx1200 / gfx1201 the engine sets five exact prompt switches on every run
+  (`STRATA_GDN_HEAD`, `STRATA_GDN_PP=2`, `STRATA_GDN_CONVL2`, `STRATA_GDN_NOY`, `STRATA_CVEC_FUSE`; #1478). With
+  `--layer-split` and two or more GPUs visible it also sets the ten exact decode switches of the gfx1151 table
+  (`STRATA_Q8_PACKED` ... `STRATA_PLE_BATCH`, not `STRATA_SH_STREAM`; list and numbers in
+  [DETAILS.md](DETAILS.md)). On one R9700 those decode switches measured slower, so a one-GPU run does not get them;
+  on 2x R9700 (`--layer-split 26`, IQ3_S, every expert resident) they took greedy decode from 108.0 to 115.0 tok/s
+  and 64K prompt reads from 2,452 to 2,792 tok/s, with byte-identical greedy output. The opt-in `STRATA_HIP_WMMA`
+  (changes bits) adds more on prompts.
+  `STRATA_GFX12_SPLIT_DECODE=0` drops the decode half, `STRATA_GFX12_DEFAULTS=0` the whole table; the start-up line
+  names what was set.
 - **Known:** rarely (about 1 start in 10) a HIP run's greedy output differs from another start's at some token, on
   one card or two and on engine 0.1.29 as well; not yet explained.
 - **Not validated:** images, long contexts beyond 16K, answer-quality benchmarks.
