From 1c7ec78011d8339d9ac5fd65963b80af08de93a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Cunningham <justin@bulletprooftiger.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:40:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] STRATA_Q8_PACKED: the split search prices the packed
 copies, and a copy that does not fit is dropped instead of aborting the load

STRATA_Q8_PACKED=1 (on by default on gfx1151) keeps a second, packed copy
of each eligible Q8_0 dense matrix in VRAM. NativeDense::load allocated
it, but NativeDense::weight_bytes_for, which prices a later stage's
projections for `--layer-split auto --trim-stage-weights` (#1238), did
not count it. The search could then give a stage more layers than its
card holds, and a failed packed cudaMalloc ended the load with "native
dense packed upload".

- weight_bytes_for adds the packed copy of every matrix that load would
  pack. One predicate (q8_packs) now serves both, so they stay in step.
- load: when the packed copy's cudaMalloc runs out of memory, the copy is
  dropped, one stderr line names the matrix, and the matrices after it
  are not packed either. The MMVQ looks each matrix up in the packed
  registry and reads the GGUF layout when there is no entry, so the
  decode output does not change, only the speed of those matrices. Any
  other error (a failed copy) still ends the load as before.
- allocated_bytes() now counts the packed copies; weight_bytes() stays
  the GGUF payload (the packed total has its own log line).

The SYCL port has its own native_dense.cpp and is not changed.

Checks: built for HIP (ROCm 7.2.4, gfx1201, Linux, GCC); no GPU run of
this commit. The packed path acts only on Q8_0 dense matrices of an
eligible shape. The IQ3_S pack's one Q8_0 projection
(blk.47.ffn_down_shexp, 640 inputs) is below the packed kernel's
minimum width, so on that pack neither change does anything.
