-**gfx12 (RDNA4): exact speed switches on by default, the decode half only for a layer split.** At start the engine looks at GPU 0. On gfx1200 / gfx1201 it sets the prompt half of the gfx1151 table (`STRATA_GDN_HEAD`, `STRATA_GDN_PP=2`, `STRATA_GDN_CONVL2`, `STRATA_GDN_NOY`, `STRATA_CVEC_FUSE`; #1478) on every run. With `--layer-split` and two or more GPUs visible it also sets the ten decode switches of that table (`STRATA_Q8_PACKED`, `STRATA_Q6_PACKED`, `STRATA_MMVF_ROWS`, `STRATA_ATTN_LANECELL`, `STRATA_EXPERT_V2`, `STRATA_TSUM`, `STRATA_LFUSE`, `STRATA_GDN_SPLIT`, `STRATA_QFUSE`, `STRATA_PLE_BATCH`; not `STRATA_SH_STREAM`). All of them are bitwise switches ([STRIX_HALO.md](STRIX_HALO.md) section 4): they change speed, not answers. On one R9700 the decode half measured slower, so a one-GPU run keeps the prompt half only. On 2x R9700 32 GB (Ryzen 9 5900X, PCIe 4.0 x8 / x8, ROCm 7.2.4), Qwen3.8-Flash-Next IQ3_S, `--layer-split 26` (every expert resident), 3 runs each, the stock prompt-only table gave greedy 108.0 tok/s (geometric mean of prose / code / edit / reasoning; mean of two sessions), sampled 100.5 tok/s and cold prompts of 4K / 16K / 64K at 1,370 / 1,553 / 2,452 tok/s; with these ten switches it gave 115.0 (+6.5%), 106.6 (+6.1%) and 1,450 / 1,788 / 2,792 (+6% / +15% / +14%), with byte-identical greedy output on all four prompts. If you accept changed bits, the opt-in `STRATA_HIP_WMMA` on top reads prompts faster still (1,759 / 2,376 / 3,556). `STRATA_GFX12_SPLIT_DECODE=0` keeps the prompt half only; `STRATA_GFX12_DEFAULTS=0` turns both off; a switch you set yourself is kept. The decision is made before the weights load, so on a box with two or more GPUs a split that ends up on one GPU (`--split-device 0`, or `--split-skip-if-fits` when the model fits) keeps the decode half.
